    "putt-water": {
      "_bug": "KNOWN DEFECT, not a sanctioned cost. 187k triangles is 17x every other putt scene, on the board that should be the cheapest thing golf ships. Cause: PuttGL.tsx builds the hazard with makeWaterPlane(..., ydPerSegment=0.12), which saturates makeWaterPlane's 160-segment clamp on BOTH axes -> 160x160 quads = 51,200 triangles for one rectangle, again per shadow and reflection pass. It buys nothing visible: the visual gate reports a flat blue rectangle with no geometric wave relief (amplitude 0.09 units under a near-overhead camera). Raising ydPerSegment to ~0.6 should cut ~40k triangles per pass with no perceptible change. This ceiling exists so the gate has a baseline to work from -- do NOT read it as approval.",
